@startuml sequence_login
title Login Flow (FR-005, SEC-005, UX-002–004)

actor User
participant Frontend
participant Backend

User -> Frontend : open login page,\nenter email + password

alt no CSRF token held in memory
  Frontend -> Backend : GET /api/v1/auth/csrf/ (credentialed)
  Backend --> Frontend : Set-Cookie: csrf cookie (HttpOnly)\nbody: { csrf_token }
  note right of Frontend
    csrf_token held only in application
    memory — never read from the cookie
  end note
end

Frontend -> Backend : POST /api/v1/auth/login/\nX-CSRFToken: <csrf_token>\nbody: { email, password }
Backend -> Backend : validate CSRF token\nvalidate credentials

alt valid credentials
  Backend --> Frontend : 200 OK\nbody: { access_token }\nSet-Cookie: refresh_token\n(HttpOnly, /api/v1/auth/)
  Frontend -> Frontend : hold access_token in memory only\nremove medical_tracker.logout_intent
  Frontend -> User : open authenticated dashboard
else unknown email OR incorrect password
  Backend --> Frontend : 401 Unauthorized\nbody: { "detail": "Invalid credentials." }
  note over Backend
    Identical response for both cases
    (ADS-SEC-006-02) — does not disclose
    whether the account exists.
  end note
  Frontend -> User : show generic authentication error
else missing / mismatched CSRF
  Backend --> Frontend : 403 Forbidden (CSRF failure)
  Frontend -> User : show error,\nno session created
end

@enduml
